# ── Chapter 13 fidelity pins: "The One Thing Taken" ──────────────────────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   nibli-pin --kb new-book-plans/utopia-v2.nibli \
#             book-1/13-the-one-thing-taken.pins.nibli
#
# Two of this chapter's claims are about ABSENCES and cannot be queried:
#   - "Nothing depends on it" — travel appears once in the constitution, as a
#     rule head. Re-check with a grep if the rules change.
#   - "There is no release" — no duration, term, expiry or completion exists in
#     any rule. Every apparent hit is commentary. If a release rule is ever
#     added, the closing section must be rewritten.

:expect-pins 13

# "Hano was convicted ... and cannot move freely."
? prisoner(Hano).
# => TRUE

? travel(Hano).
# => FALSE

# The audit, item by item — everything else Hano keeps
? person(Hano).
# => TRUE

? expresses(Hano).
# => TRUE

? decide(Hano, Ballot).
# => TRUE

? false(Hano).
# => FALSE

? lose(Points, Hano).
# => FALSE

? dwell(Hano).
# => TRUE

# "the difference between Hano and Jala, who did the same thing to the same
#  person and was never convicted"
? injure(Jala, Ivo).
# => TRUE

? prisoner(Jala).
# => FALSE

? travel(Jala).
# => TRUE

# Voiding is not confinement: Bela lost standing and still moves
? false(Bela).
# => TRUE

? travel(Bela).
# => TRUE
